From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:04:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Scale-weight diagnostics: projected radius, scale weight and
 unweighted score

- sim_diag_accum (radius, scale weight, unweighted view score over valid views) replaces
  sim_radius_accum; fed by train_sim.py and train_sim_rendersim.py
- utils/scale_weight_stats.py: interval membership with / without the scale weight,
  transition matrix, fraction of large Gaussians per interval, "G3 only by scale weight"
- save_similarity_scale_statistics_json records these fields (subsampled, compact JSON)
- train_sim.py --sem_log adds the summary to sem_log.jsonl and npz snapshots
- similarity_scale_scatter.py plots similarity vs radius, unweighted vs weighted score,
  radius distributions, and the previous scale-ratio scatter

